              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for to fold, then the Persian for to hang up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: داد زدن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "داد زدن — dâd zadan — \"to shout\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dâd zadan pairs dâd, \"cry\", with zadan, \"to strike\". dâd is the old word for \"justice\" (Middle Persian dād, \"law, justice\", EtymDB), and a shout is usually explained as first a cry for justice. zadan, \"to strike\", is an inherited verb; it is usually traced to Middle Persian zadan."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
